  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Shared park Q505617 identifies the site; independent way412339872/native35184784428704 identifies this separate southern polygonal latrine. Its eight mapped vertices set meter scale and offsets. Internal +X points east-southeast away from the villa and +Z follows the western side south-southwest. Native east/up/south axes are baked with heading 0. Only this one footprint is replaced; the northern eastern latrine and every other building remain independent.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Photo-led medium-fi surviving masonry exterior. Existing ordinary aerial shows this southern detached polygon as an open dark center bounded by a low pale rim, beside the southern apartments and inside the path. No roof covers that visible center. Exact mapped outer polygon sets scale; inner face is a reconstructed 0.79 radial inset. Working wall tops vary 0.88–1.12m above local original terrain. Wall heights, west gap position/width, thickness, fracture pattern and unseen faces are unmeasured approximations. No qualified map height; exact excavated floor/paving, benches/drains and accessibility are unverified. No roof, mosaic copy, furnished interior or subterranean reconstruction."
  },
